# Memory and Tools Rules

Memory defaults:

- Memory is enabled by default.
- Store summaries and preferences.
- Do not store raw transcripts by default.
- Support inspection and forgetting.

Minimum memory schema:

- `preferences`
- `memory_items`
- `conversation_summaries`
- `tool_approvals`
- `approved_paths`

Tool defaults:

- Tool system may be scaffolded in v0.1 but dangerous tools must not be enabled without permission gates.
- Every tool has a permission class.
- Every sensitive action requires approval.
- Every action should produce audit metadata.

Tools desired eventually:

- read files;
- search folders;
- summarize PDFs/docs;
- write Markdown notes;
- create project files;
- run shell commands;
- open apps;
- edit code;
- manage calendar;
- draft emails;
- send emails;
- browse web.

Allowed default folder:

```text
C:\Users\DELL\Documents\GitHub\ProjectAtticus
```

Even inside the repo, shell commands and file edits still need confirmation in user-facing operation. Automated tests may write only to test temp directories.
